steps.body:
Some windows have no fixed size: you want the longest or shortest run that follows a rule. Grow the window by moving `right` one step every pass. When the new value breaks the rule, shrink it from the left with a `while` loop until the rule holds again. Each index enters once and leaves once, so it's still one pass.

For the longest stretch of a string with no repeated character, a `HashSet` holds the window's characters:

```java
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Set;

String s = "abcabcbb";
Set<Character> window = new HashSet<>();
int left = 0;
int best = 0;
for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {
    char c = s.charAt(right);
    while (window.contains(c)) {
        window.remove(s.charAt(left));   // shrink until c is gone
        left++;
    }
    window.add(c);
    best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
}
System.out.println(best); // 3
```

The window runs from `left` to `right`, so its length is `right - left + 1`. Use `while`, not `if`: the repeat may sit several places in, and every character before it has to leave too.

Shrinking only works when dropping values from the left can fix the rule. For a sum limit, that holds when the values are never negative, since dropping one can only lower the sum.

example.code:
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Scanner;
import java.util.Set;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        while (sc.hasNext()) {
            String s = sc.next();
            Set<Character> window = new HashSet<>();
            int left = 0;
            int best = 0;
            int bestStart = 0;
            for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {
                char c = s.charAt(right);
                while (window.contains(c)) {
                    window.remove(s.charAt(left));
                    left++;
                }
                window.add(c);
                if (right - left + 1 > best) {
                    best = right - left + 1;
                    bestStart = left;
                }
            }
            System.out.println(s + ": " + best + " " + s.substring(bestStart, bestStart + best));
        }
    }
}

