steps.body:
Keep a running total `sum` of everything so far. The subarray after index `j` up to index `i` adds up to the total at `i` minus the total at `j`. So a subarray that ends here sums to `k` exactly when some earlier running total equals `sum - k`. Keep a map from each running total to how many times you have seen it:

```java
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

int[] nums = {1, 2, 1, 2, 1};
int k = 3;
Map<Integer, Integer> seen = new HashMap<>();
seen.put(0, 1);                              // the empty start, before index 0
int sum = 0;
int count = 0;
for (int x : nums) {
    sum += x;
    count += seen.getOrDefault(sum - k, 0);  // earlier totals that leave exactly k
    seen.merge(sum, 1, Integer::sum);
}
System.out.println(count); // 4
```

`seen.put(0, 1)` lets a subarray that starts at index 0 count. Look up `sum - k` before you add the current total, or a subarray of length 0 counts when `k` is 0.

Unlike a sliding window, this works with negative numbers, because it never assumes that a longer window has a bigger sum. Running totals can outgrow an `int` on long inputs, so switch to `long` and a `Map<Long, Integer>` when they might.

example.code:
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        int[] nums = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            nums[i] = sc.nextInt();
        }
        int k = sc.nextInt();

        Map<Integer, Integer> seen = new HashMap<>();
        seen.put(0, 1);
        int sum = 0;
        int count = 0;
        StringBuilder totals = new StringBuilder("Running totals:");
        for (int x : nums) {
            sum += x;
            totals.append(' ').append(sum);
            count += seen.getOrDefault(sum - k, 0);
            seen.merge(sum, 1, Integer::sum);
        }
        System.out.println(totals);
        System.out.println("Subarrays summing to " + k + ": " + count);
    }
}

